# SFX stays on presentation helpers

Player-facing sounds live in `Sfx.play()` / `Sfx.play_effectiveness()`. Call them from the helper that already owns the visual, never from a `Button.pressed` handler or a one-off screen script.

Canonical hooks (do not bypass):

- Attack / Special → `AnimaPresenter.play_fx()`
- Guard → `AnimaPresenter.guard_shimmer()`
- Feed / battle item → `AnimaPresenter.care_feedback()`
- Super effective / not very effective → `AnimaPresenter.hit_react(multiplier)`
- Summon + Switch portal → `IncubatorEffect.start_portal()`
- Level Up → `scan_flow._present_level_up_outcome()` when its FIFO item is shown
- Synthesis/Evolution complete → `scan_flow._present_next_outcome_dialog()` when a success item is shown (same cue as Level Up)
- Chrome taps → `UiJuice` (`button_down`)

If you restyle a button or move a dock, leave these helpers in the play path. `test_scan_ui.gd` source-scans the hooks; a missing `Sfx.play` is a failed check, not a later TODO.
